claim.claim-text:
contacting the hydrocarbon mixture with a 10-ring pore molecular sieve at a temperature of -20°C to 60 °C for a time and under conditions to provide a sieved hydrocarbon mixture comprising the cyclic olefin;
contacting the sieved hydrocarbon mixture with a polymerization catalyst for a time and under conditions to polymerize the cyclic olefin, thereby forming the hydrocarbon polymer;
wherein the 10-ring pore molecular sieve has:

a sieving channel with a 10-ring sieving aperture with a minimum crystallographic free diameter greater than 3Å and a ratio of the maximum crystallographic free diameter to the minimum crystallographic free diameter between 1 and 2;
a T1/T2 ratio ≥ 20:1, wherein T1 is an element independently selected from Si, Ge and a combination thereof, and T2 is an element independently selected from Al, B, Ga and a combination thereof; and
a counterion selected from NH<4>+
